# Divide and Conquer, Sorting and Searching, and Randomized Algorithms

This repository contains Python implementations of core algorithms from the first course of Stanford University's *Algorithms Specialization* (taught by Prof. Tim Roughgarden, offered via Coursera). It was developed as part of my independent study of algorithm design and analysis, with an emphasis on the divide-and-conquer paradigm, classical sorting/searching techniques, and randomized algorithms.

Each implementation includes:
- A clear docstring explaining the underlying algorithmic idea
- Time (and, where relevant, space) complexity analysis
- Self-contained test cases with correctness checks (`assert` statements)

## 🎓 Certificate

This work reflects material covered in the course, which I completed and was awarded a certificate for:

[![Coursera Certificate](https://img.shields.io/badge/Coursera-Certificate-blue?logo=coursera)](https://www.coursera.org/account/accomplishments/certificate/DMIUVGHBK2GT)

